ad but  at the very least gauche and gray are  now established gordon friends whether  they like it  or not but now we move on to expanding  into some other nations something i  really enjoyed because i am a big big  big fan of world building  something that most shonen series  honestly really suck at  and black bull it's not the best but i  will take what i can get and what we get  is a very sudden excursion to the heart  kingdom  actually i don't think sudden quite  expresses the feeling well enough  because we basically go from oh mimosa  you've been to the heart kingdom before  right to turning a page and we're all  just immediately within the heart  kingdom like it's no big deal  holy crap that was fast anyway i do like  that the heart kingdom has a distinct  culture of its own at least when it  comes to magic and mana use which  introduces us to another great spirit  actually undine who is kind of like self  but  bigger and water related which i imagine  is meant to be pretty  impressive right like if the salamander  situation was anything to go by the size  of the spirit is pretty much a direct  indication of how much of their power is  able to be utilized  maybe i don't know that's just the  impression i have at the moment either  way there's some you know impressive  crap happening in the hot kingdom most  of which is handled by this really  awkward queen which is also fun  and it's it's kind of cliche but i'm  glad she isn't a standard stoic  power queen as well sort of like the  witch queen although to be fair that  witch queen  oh she's cool still easily one of my  favorite characters in the series we do  have  problems though as per usual one of  which is that our queen of hearts is  cursed by the ever fiendish  and will die within a year that sounds  pretty bad  and as such we are teaming up with the  clover kingdom sort of which i liked the  reasoning behind by the way the whole  idea that for as powerful as these heart  kingdom dude bras are their magical  evolution is just completely  incompatible with the idea of fighting  devils so they need to rely on these  very obscure  brands of clover kingdom magic that have  popped up like yummy's dark magic  oh and before moving on we have a new  magic ranking system as well  something simultaneously less and yet  somehow more vague than the magic knight  ranking system the heart kingdom do  things by levels a system that is also  immediately broken by the idea of level  zero and arcane level that i like stuff  like this regardless i crave structure i  demand it and sadly the magic knight  system gave me very little of that it  was exciting at first before all of the  ranks were rendered  pretty much irrelevant and i think this  system will probably follow along the  same lines just  knowing black clover at this stage but  let's go with it for now especially  since noel is a glorious stage one and  is now casually sporting that valkyrie  armor doing exactly what i wanted her to  do by the way thrusting herself onto the  front lines and no longer having to act  as a mere support mage she is just so  legitimately amazing now like the  magical equivalent of astor but getting  into big news the most intriguing  information comes from the spade kingdom  who appeared to be our new long-term bad  guys now the elves are well they're no  longer a thing in fact we didn't even  know what happened to paltry and the  the three dude brows at this point they  just vanished huh didn't even think  about that until now but the spade guys  are immediately highlighted as quite  serious business because for the first  time in human  history luck does not want to fight  someone a spade kingdom representative  that he spots whilst keeping an eye on  the diamond kingdom pretty scary stuff i  suppose but naturally we do need to  escalate the threat which  is a bit of a difficult thing to do  after having faced off against this  impossibly powerful band of elves as  well as an infinitely power